From: pmOS Q706F fixes
Subject: [PATCH] HID: i2c-hid: Elan 04F3:31F3 BAD_INPUT_SIZE

The Q706F folio touchpad interrupts but i2c-hid drops the packets as
"incomplete report" (short length vs parsed wMaxInputLength). Accept
the size in the I2C prefix, matching other ITE/Elan I2C-HID devices.

Keep the existing ELAN NO_WAKEUP_AFTER_RESET and BOGUS_IRQ flags.

---
--- a/drivers/hid/i2c-hid/i2c-hid-core.c
+++ b/drivers/hid/i2c-hid/i2c-hid-core.c
@@ -147,6 +147,10 @@
 	{ USB_VENDOR_ID_ELAN, HID_ANY_ID,
 		 I2C_HID_QUIRK_NO_WAKEUP_AFTER_RESET |
 		 I2C_HID_QUIRK_BOGUS_IRQ },
+	{ USB_VENDOR_ID_ELAN, 0x31f3,
+		 I2C_HID_QUIRK_NO_WAKEUP_AFTER_RESET |
+		 I2C_HID_QUIRK_BOGUS_IRQ |
+		 I2C_HID_QUIRK_BAD_INPUT_SIZE },
 	{ I2C_VENDOR_ID_GOODIX, I2C_DEVICE_ID_GOODIX_0D42,
 		 I2C_HID_QUIRK_DELAY_WAKEUP_AFTER_RESUME },
 	{ I2C_VENDOR_ID_BLTP, I2C_PRODUCT_ID_BLTP7853,
